{0 Hamlet automatic propagation subtraction}

Write [\[%hamlet.propagate_e.auto\]] in a [Combinators.catch] handler or
[\[%hamlet.propagate_s.auto\]] in a [Combinators.provide] handler. The configured
[hamlet-subtractor.ppx] path types a temporary probe from the current source
and already-built interfaces, proves a finite exact input row, and returns
final ordinary OCaml propagation cases before normal type checking. Merlin
therefore types the same final expansion as Dune and shows the precise effect
type. When the proof is unavailable, the marker receives an actionable
diagnostic asking for an explicit [\[%hamlet.te ...\]] or [\[%hamlet.ts ...\]]
boundary.

{1 Components}

- {!Hamlet_subtractor_core} contains compiler-independent identities, proofs,
  residual calculations, diagnostics, and effect certificates.
- {!Hamlet_subtractor_engine} schedules dependent markers deterministically
  while preserving exact evidence for both Hamlet channels.
- {!Hamlet_subtractor_generator} creates type-safe final forwarding cases,
  including linear [Errors.Cases] dispatch for verified complete catalogues.
